as evidence.","outcome_codes":["EN4-ECA-01"],"parent_notes":"Parent: Marking guidance for the independent task: Independently draft a suspense scene (180–220 words) with annotated plant/delay/payoff, then revise pacing in one paragraph using sentence-length contrast. Accept equivalent original responses that show the same skill.\n\nParent: Written model 1: Sample: original example using suspense on new material; names a specific word, source or choice and explains its effect.\n\nParent: Written model 2: Sample error: Withholding so much that readers are confused rather than curious, or resolving every thread in the same sentence.. Correction: Strong answer: question clear;. Why it helps the audience is stated.\n\nParent: Likely misconception: Withholding so much that readers are confused rather than curious, or resolving every thread in the same sentence. Keep sample answers out of the child role.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 1: Produce a fresh example demonstrating suspense on new material (not the worked model). Explain the particular words, sources or choices that make it work.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 2: Name one likely error with suspense, correct it, and explain why the correction helps a reader or audience.\n\nParent: Marking notes: Accept original work about suspense with a specific supporting detail. Reject copied model wording with no new material. / Accept a misconception, a correction, and a purpose-linked reason for suspense. Reject corrections that do not change the inaccurate idea..","pass":1,"pass_mark":0.9,"planner_fields":null,"planner_intro":null,"planner_title":null,"printable_resource":null,"quiz":[{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"This matches the taught method for suspense. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Ignore the words and invent a more exciting event.","Skip the prompt because the first idea sounded good.","question clear; delay purposeful; payoff incomplete but earned.","Withholding so much that readers are confused rather than curious, or resolving every thread in the same sentence."],"question":"Write a 120-word suspense beat that plants one question, delays it, and lands a partial payoff without resolving everything. Which response is most accurate?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"This is the misconception to avoid for suspense; the other choices align with the lesson method. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Withholding so much that readers are confused rather than curious, or resolving every thread in the same sentence.","Writing suspense raises stakes and controls information: readers know enough to care and not enough to relax.","question clear; delay purposeful; payoff incomplete but earned.","Careful use of withholding with clear evidence."],"question":"Which statement is a common mistake when working with suspense?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"Understanding is shown by new evidence and a named withholding, not by copying the model. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Withholding so much that readers are confused rather than curious, or resolving every thread in the same sentence.","Name withholding only, without linking it to suspense.","Apply suspense to new material and name the withholding used.","Repeat the worked example wording with no new evidence."],"question":"Which response best applies suspense with new evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"The skill is shown by quoting or pointing to wording that carries suspense. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Withholding so much that readers are confused rather than curious, or resolving every thread in the same sentence.","Point to exact words in the sentence that show suspense and say what they do.","Ignore the sentence and invent a more exciting event.","Say the writing is good without naming any words."],"question":"Read: \"After the blackout, Tess lit a candle and read the crumpled note.\" Which choice best uses suspense from this lesson?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"The correct statement applies the language skill with textual evidence. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["question clear; delay purposeful; payoff incomplete but earned.","Withholding so much that readers are confused rather than curious, or resolving every thread in the same sentence.","Copy a model sentence from another story unchanged.","Name withholding without linking it to any words in the text."],"question":"Which statement correctly applies the lesson idea about suspense?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"Start from a specific textual clue, then explain its effect. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Guess from the title alone with no textual clue.","Copy a model sentence from another story unchanged.","Lengthen the answer with adjectives while keeping the same idea.","Locate precise textual evidence, then explain how language choices shape meaning or effect."],"question":"In a new text, what should you do first to analyse withholding?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Repair means fixing meaning or evidence, not padding. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Delete the evidence that disagreed with your first guess.","Change the inaccurate idea or missing evidence, not only the length.","Add adjectives without fixing the wrong idea.","Make the answer longer while keeping the same mistake."],"question":"Which revision actually improves meaning for suspense?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Accurate transfer needs fresh material with an explained language choice. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Withholding so much that readers are confused rather than curious, or resolving every thread in the same sentence.","Use a fresh sentence or text and explain one precise choice about suspense.","Retype the worked model as the final answer.","Change fonts and claim the work is new."],"question":"Which response shows accurate use of suspense on fresh material?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"explanation":"Independent evidence on new material demonstrates the skill; copying the model does not.","marking_guide":"Accept original work about suspense with a specific supporting detail. Reject copied model wording with no new material.","question":"Produce a fresh example demonstrating suspense on new material (not the worked model). Explain the particular words, sources or choices that make it work.","sample_answer":"Sample: original example using suspense on new material; names a specific word, source or choice and explains its effect.","type":"short_answer"},{"explanation":"A useful correction changes the inaccurate idea or method and explains why.","marking_guide":"Accept a misconception, a correction, and a purpose-linked reason for suspense. Reject corrections that do not change the inaccurate idea.","question":"Name one likely error with suspense, correct it, and explain why the correction helps a reader or audience.","sample_answer":"Sample error: Withholding so much that readers are confused rather than curious, or resolving every thread in the same sentence.. Correction: Strong answer: question clear;. Why it helps the audience is stated.","type":"short_answer"}],"resources":null,"response_prompt":"Include your independent task and reflection, with explanations where requested.","review_status":"unreviewed","seed_key":"s4-eng-y8-w03-l2","sort_activity":null,"source_note":"Proposed Stage 2 NESA alignment; verify content points before acceptance.","spelling":null,"spelling_focus":null,"stage":"S4","stage_hints":{"accept":["Today you will practise suspense.","Read the mission before you start writi